		"f1e2bbd3-9c52-45af-a263-91b5e2ba4819": {
			"path": "f1e2bbd3-9c52-45af-a263-91b5e2ba4819",
			"cellName": "Initiate Assembly - CPUDisassembly.cpp:L904-908",
			"cellId": "f1e2bbd3-9c52-45af-a263-91b5e2ba4819",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "a3b93b47-7069-4dc9-b297-300ecab13cc5"
		},
		"src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp-simstep-8cb6bd78-69a3-44de-890d-e07a170e6385": {
			"path": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp-simstep-8cb6bd78-69a3-44de-890d-e07a170e6385",
			"fileName": "CPUDisassembly.cpp",
			"wiki": "The user right-clicks on an instruction in the CPU Disassembly view and selects 'Assemble' from the context menu. This action triggers the assembleSlot, which begins the process of modifying the instruction at the selected address.",
			"cellName": "Initiate Assembly - CPUDisassembly.cpp:L904-908",
			"cellId": "f1e2bbd3-9c52-45af-a263-91b5e2ba4819",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 904,
			"endLine": 908,
			"parentCellId": "a3b93b47-7069-4dc9-b297-300ecab13cc5",
			"parentPath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "Binary Patching and In-Memory Modification",
					"simStepId": "8cb6bd78-69a3-44de-890d-e07a170e6385"
				}
			]
		},
		"5160b84c-af86-4d34-b7a8-85b6b8194c53": {
			"path": "5160b84c-af86-4d34-b7a8-85b6b8194c53",
			"cellName": "User Provides Assembly Code - AssembleDialog.cpp:L85-114",
			"cellId": "5160b84c-af86-4d34-b7a8-85b6b8194c53",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "23e3910e-68b9-4f7c-8bb9-9cdfe8b0a426"
		},
		"src/gui/Src/Gui/AssembleDialog.cpp-simstep-ee7c9286-ae00-4a43-8c63-0618271643da": {
			"path": "src/gui/Src/Gui/AssembleDialog.cpp-simstep-ee7c9286-ae00-4a43-8c63-0618271643da",
			"fileName": "AssembleDialog.cpp",
			"wiki": "The user types a new instruction (e.g., \"NOP\") into the `AssembleDialog`. The dialog validates the instruction in real-time by calling `validateInstruction`, which uses the `DbgFunctions()->Assemble` bridge function to check the syntax and calculate the size of the resulting machine code.",
			"cellName": "User Provides Assembly Code - AssembleDialog.cpp:L85-114",
			"cellId": "5160b84c-af86-4d34-b7a8-85b6b8194c53",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 85,
			"endLine": 114,
			"parentCellId": "23e3910e-68b9-4f7c-8bb9-9cdfe8b0a426",
			"parentPath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/AssembleDialog.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "Binary Patching and In-Memory Modification",
					"simStepId": "ee7c9286-ae00-4a43-8c63-0618271643da"
				}
			]
		},
		"094d8a38-f27b-44dc-8541-09e6a9d1503a": {
			"path": "094d8a38-f27b-44dc-8541-09e6a9d1503a",
			"cellName": "GUI Requests Memory Patch - CPUDisassembly.cpp:L935-938",
			"cellId": "094d8a38-f27b-44dc-8541-09e6a9d1503a",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "a3b93b47-7069-4dc9-b297-300ecab13cc5"
		},
		"src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp-simstep-4a043586-eedd-472f-b31f-6002462fd797": {
			"path": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp-simstep-4a043586-eedd-472f-b31f-6002462fd797",
			"fileName": "CPUDisassembly.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `assembleSlot` in the GUI receives the new instruction and calls `DbgFunctions()->AssembleAtEx`. This function acts as a bridge to the debugger core, requesting it to assemble the instruction and patch it into the debuggee's memory at the specified address.",
			"cellName": "GUI Requests Memory Patch - CPUDisassembly.cpp:L935-938",
			"cellId": "094d8a38-f27b-44dc-8541-09e6a9d1503a",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 935,
			"endLine": 938,
			"parentCellId": "a3b93b47-7069-4dc9-b297-300ecab13cc5",
			"parentPath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "Binary Patching and In-Memory Modification",
					"simStepId": "4a043586-eedd-472f-b31f-6002462fd797"
				}
			]
		},
		"4f01cd92-3313-42a1-9b82-105d775a5594": {
			"path": "4f01cd92-3313-42a1-9b82-105d775a5594",
			"cellName": "Core Assembles and Patches Memory - assemble.cpp:L99-156",
			"cellId": "4f01cd92-3313-42a1-9b82-105d775a5594",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "c37b5b6e-c6ca-4922-a498-150a1e005234"
		},
		"src/dbg/assemble.cpp-simstep-8d0e73e0-40e3-475d-952b-8c49dbba7c0a": {
			"path": "src/dbg/assemble.cpp-simstep-8d0e73e0-40e3-475d-952b-8c49dbba7c0a",
			"fileName": "assemble.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `assembleat` function in the debugger core is executed. It first calls `assemble` to convert the mnemonic into machine code. Then, it calls `MemPatch` to write the new bytes into the target process's memory and optionally fills the remaining space with NOPs.",
			"cellName": "Core Assembles and Patches Memory - assemble.cpp:L99-156",
			"cellId": "4f01cd92-3313-42a1-9b82-105d775a5594",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 99,
			"endLine": 156,
			"parentCellId": "c37b5b6e-c6ca-4922-a498-150a1e005234",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/assemble.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "Binary Patching and In-Memory Modification",
					"simStepId": "8d0e73e0-40e3-475d-952b-8c49dbba7c0a"
				}
			]
		},
		"cf7957d0-3280-4735-8be7-c3a11397534b": {
			"path": "cf7957d0-3280-4735-8be7-c3a11397534b",
			"cellName": "Store Patch in Internal Map - patches.cpp:L11-60",
			"cellId": "cf7957d0-3280-4735-8be7-c3a11397534b",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "977bf3da-9f3e-4acf-ae85-ddda34b872b6"
		},
		"src/dbg/patches.cpp-simstep-98532282-a66d-4cbb-ad7d-fe8af0cfbbaa": {
			"path": "src/dbg/patches.cpp-simstep-98532282-a66d-4cbb-ad7d-fe8af0cfbbaa",
			"fileName": "patches.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `PatchSet` function receives the modification details and stores them in a global `std::unordered_map<duint, PATCHINFO>` named `patches`. This map serves as the central database for all in-memory modifications made during the debugging session.",
			"cellName": "Store Patch in Internal Map - patches.cpp:L11-60",
			"cellId": "cf7957d0-3280-4735-8be7-c3a11397534b",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 11,
			"endLine": 60,
			"parentCellId": "977bf3da-9f3e-4acf-ae85-ddda34b872b6",
			"parentPath": "src/dbg/patches.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "Binary Patching and In-Memory Modification",
					"simStepId": "98532282-a66d-4cbb-ad7d-fe8af0cfbbaa"
				}
			]
		},
		"dfa0c3f3-92f9-4392-8dcf-a8e3017aa67a": {
			"path": "dfa0c3f3-92f9-4392-8dcf-a8e3017aa67a",
			"cellName": "User Opens Patches Dialog - PatchDialog.cpp:L19-20",
			"cellId": "dfa0c3f3-92f9-4392-8dcf-a8e3017aa67a",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "d62ef82d-d2bf-4d04-8c80-837253eb26fe"
		},
		"src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp-simstep-b5291a29-8a69-4e54-9148-87d9fc2db162": {
			"path": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp-simstep-b5291a29-8a69-4e54-9148-87d9fc2db162",
			"fileName": "PatchDialog.cpp",
			"wiki": "The user opens the 'Patches' dialog. The dialog's constructor connects to the `updatePatches` signal from the bridge. Upon showing, it calls `updatePatches()` to populate itself with the current patch data from the debugger core.",
			"cellName": "User Opens Patches Dialog - PatchDialog.cpp:L19-20",
			"cellId": "dfa0c3f3-92f9-4392-8dcf-a8e3017aa67a",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 19,
			"endLine": 20,
			"parentCellId": "d62ef82d-d2bf-4d04-8c80-837253eb26fe",
			"parentPath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "Binary Patching and In-Memory Modification",
					"simStepId": "b5291a29-8a69-4e54-9148-87d9fc2db162"
				}
			]
		},
		"929af388-72f2-4739-a703-cb29da38cf95": {
			"path": "929af388-72f2-4739-a703-cb29da38cf95",
			"cellName": "Core Gathers Patch Information - patches.cpp:L153-178",
			"cellId": "929af388-72f2-4739-a703-cb29da38cf95",
			"visible": true,
			"parentCellId": "977bf3da-9f3e-4acf-ae85-ddda34b872b6"
		},
		"src/dbg/patches.cpp-simstep-6191ef16-1f19-44d3-9419-95dec55272bd": {
			"path": "src/dbg/patches.cpp-simstep-6191ef16-1f19-44d3-9419-95dec55272bd",
			"fileName": "patches.cpp",
			"wiki": "The `PatchEnum` function in the debugger core is executed. It iterates over its internal `patches` map and copies the information for each recorded patch into the list structure provided by the GUI.",
			"cellName": "Core Gathers Patch Information - patches.cpp:L153-178",
			"cellId": "929af388-72f2-4739-a703-cb29da38cf95",
			"visible": true,
