		"Binary Patching and In-Memory Modification": {
			"name": "Binary Patching and In-Memory Modification",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "8cb6bd78-69a3-44de-890d-e07a170e6385",
					"diagramNodeId": "f1e2bbd3-9c52-45af-a263-91b5e2ba4819",
					"simStepLabel": "Initiate Assembly",
					"simStepDescription": "The user right-clicks on an instruction in the CPU Disassembly view and selects 'Assemble' from the context menu. This action triggers the assembleSlot, which begins the process of modifying the instruction at the selected address.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp",
						"startLine": "904",
						"endLine": "908",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"CPUDisassembly::assembleSlot"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"user_action\": \"Right-click -> Assemble\", \"selected_address\": \"0x00401050\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "df612297-3e7c-475b-81fb-4ae10c3e01a7",
					"diagramNodeId": "e8871c91-82ff-45b6-8f2f-9082656da635",
					"simStepLabel": "Open Assemble Dialog",
					"simStepDescription": "The `assembleSlot` function creates an `AssembleDialog`, sets its initial state including the address to assemble at and the current instruction text, and then displays it to the user.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp",
						"startLine": "906",
						"endLine": "921",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"assembleDialog"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"va\": \"0x00401050\", \"current_instruction\": \"MOV EAX, EBX\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"va\": \"0x00401050\", \"current_instruction\": \"MOV EAX, EBX\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ee7c9286-ae00-4a43-8c63-0618271643da",
					"diagramNodeId": "5160b84c-af86-4d34-b7a8-85b6b8194c53",
					"simStepLabel": "User Provides Assembly Code",
					"simStepDescription": "The user types a new instruction (e.g., \"NOP\") into the `AssembleDialog`. The dialog validates the instruction in real-time by calling `validateInstruction`, which uses the `DbgFunctions()->Assemble` bridge function to check the syntax and calculate the size of the resulting machine code.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/AssembleDialog.cpp",
						"startLine": "85",
						"endLine": "114",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"AssembleDialog::validateInstruction",
							"DbgFunctions()->Assemble"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"user_input_text\": \"NOP\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"validation_result\": \"OK\", \"instruction_size\": 1, \"opcode\": \"90\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "ae11d354-cf48-467d-a771-1b7f19dbc46c",
					"diagramNodeId": "46162a06-9715-460b-820b-4433218b672b",
					"simStepLabel": "Submit New Instruction",
					"simStepDescription": "The user clicks the 'OK' button. The `AssembleDialog` closes, and the new instruction text ('NOP'), along with options like 'Fill with NOPs', is returned to the calling `assembleSlot` function in `CPUDisassembly`.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp",
						"startLine": "923",
						"endLine": "932",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"assembleDialog.exec()",
							"expression"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"instruction\": \"NOP\", \"fillWithNops\": true, \"keepSize\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"instruction\": \"NOP\", \"fillWithNops\": true, \"keepSize\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "4a043586-eedd-472f-b31f-6002462fd797",
					"diagramNodeId": "094d8a38-f27b-44dc-8541-09e6a9d1503a",
					"simStepLabel": "GUI Requests Memory Patch",
					"simStepDescription": "The `assembleSlot` in the GUI receives the new instruction and calls `DbgFunctions()->AssembleAtEx`. This function acts as a bridge to the debugger core, requesting it to assemble the instruction and patch it into the debuggee's memory at the specified address.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/CPUDisassembly.cpp",
						"startLine": "935",
						"endLine": "938",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgFunctions()->AssembleAtEx",
							"va",
							"expression"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"va\": \"0x00401050\", \"instruction\": \"NOP\", \"fillWithNops\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"status\": \"pending_assembly\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "0f63b802-8efc-4494-91b9-a0615ad134a3",
					"diagramNodeId": "a3ebe90a-63eb-42bf-91e1-786e4d56b25d",
					"simStepLabel": "Transmit Assembly Request to Debugger Core",
					"simStepDescription": "The `AssembleAtEx` call crosses the bridge from the GUI component to the debugger (DBG) component. The parameters (address, instruction string, and flags) are passed to the `assembleat` function in the core.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/_dbgfunctions.cpp",
						"startLine": "115",
						"endLine": "118",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"_dbgfunctions.AssembleAtEx",
							"assembleat"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"instruction\": \"NOP\", \"fillnop\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"instruction\": \"NOP\", \"fillnop\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "8d0e73e0-40e3-475d-952b-8c49dbba7c0a",
					"diagramNodeId": "4f01cd92-3313-42a1-9b82-105d775a5594",
					"simStepLabel": "Core Assembles and Patches Memory",
					"simStepDescription": "The `assembleat` function in the debugger core is executed. It first calls `assemble` to convert the mnemonic into machine code. Then, it calls `MemPatch` to write the new bytes into the target process's memory and optionally fills the remaining space with NOPs.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/assemble.cpp",
						"startLine": "99",
						"endLine": "156",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"assembleat",
							"assemble",
							"MemPatch"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"instruction\": \"NOP\", \"fillnop\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"bytes_written\": 1, \"opcodes\": \"90\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "5ed7bbf8-fede-4445-a40a-e802bafe89bc",
					"diagramNodeId": "34f95a78-3fe2-4b18-9f74-00581d300a77",
					"simStepLabel": "Record Patch Details",
					"simStepDescription": "Within the `MemPatch` function, a call is made to `PatchSet` for each modified byte. This function is responsible for recording the change, storing the address, module name, original byte, and the newly written byte.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/memory.cpp",
						"startLine": "766",
						"endLine": "767",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"PatchSet"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"Address\": \"0x00401050\", \"OldByte\": \"0x8B\", \"NewByte\": \"0x90\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"Address\": \"0x00401050\", \"OldByte\": \"0x8B\", \"NewByte\": \"0x90\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "98532282-a66d-4cbb-ad7d-fe8af0cfbbaa",
					"diagramNodeId": "cf7957d0-3280-4735-8be7-c3a11397534b",
					"simStepLabel": "Store Patch in Internal Map",
					"simStepDescription": "The `PatchSet` function receives the modification details and stores them in a global `std::unordered_map<duint, PATCHINFO>` named `patches`. This map serves as the central database for all in-memory modifications made during the debugging session.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/patches.cpp",
						"startLine": "11",
						"endLine": "60",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"PatchSet",
							"patches",
							"newPatch"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"Address\": \"0x00401050\", \"OldByte\": \"0x8B\", \"NewByte\": \"0x90\", \"Module\": \"test.exe\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"status\": \"Patch information stored successfully\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "20ff68ca-6df9-4c1c-b247-1a3fc3428cf5",
					"diagramNodeId": "e964115d-9352-45df-9df3-c28b644bd469",
					"simStepLabel": "Notify UI of Changes",
					"simStepDescription": "After the memory is patched and recorded, `assembleat` calls `GuiUpdatePatches()` and `GuiUpdateAllViews()`. This sends a signal across the bridge to the GUI, instructing it to refresh all relevant views to reflect the changes.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/assemble.cpp",
						"startLine": "151",
						"endLine": "151",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"GuiUpdatePatches"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b5291a29-8a69-4e54-9148-87d9fc2db162",
					"diagramNodeId": "dfa0c3f3-92f9-4392-8dcf-a8e3017aa67a",
					"simStepLabel": "User Opens Patches Dialog",
					"simStepDescription": "The user opens the 'Patches' dialog. The dialog's constructor connects to the `updatePatches` signal from the bridge. Upon showing, it calls `updatePatches()` to populate itself with the current patch data from the debugger core.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp",
						"startLine": "19",
						"endLine": "20",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"PatchDialog::PatchDialog",
							"Bridge::getBridge",
							"updatePatches"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"user_action\": \"View -> Patches\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6e272829-1b7e-4d7d-9a59-90024054df24",
					"diagramNodeId": "d6900988-afd7-47b1-8f80-03266903411e",
					"simStepLabel": "GUI Requests Patch List from Core",
					"simStepDescription": "The `updatePatches` method calls `DbgFunctions()->PatchEnum` to send a request across the bridge to the debugger core, asking for a complete list of all active patches.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp",
						"startLine": "102",
						"endLine": "103",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgFunctions()->PatchEnum"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "6191ef16-1f19-44d3-9419-95dec55272bd",
					"diagramNodeId": "929af388-72f2-4739-a703-cb29da38cf95",
					"simStepLabel": "Core Gathers Patch Information",
					"simStepDescription": "The `PatchEnum` function in the debugger core is executed. It iterates over its internal `patches` map and copies the information for each recorded patch into the list structure provided by the GUI.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/dbg/patches.cpp",
						"startLine": "153",
						"endLine": "178",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"PatchEnum",
							"patches",
							"List"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"patch_count\": 1, \"patches\": [{\"mod\": \"test.exe\", \"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"oldbyte\": \"0x8B\", \"newbyte\": \"0x90\"}]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "b15eb59c-ee48-4950-b2bf-e889c0570559",
					"diagramNodeId": "ea60c087-a972-43c3-a766-760e0075c531",
					"simStepLabel": "Patches List Sent to GUI",
					"simStepDescription": "The populated list of `DBGPATCHINFO` structures is returned from the debugger core back to the `PatchDialog` in the GUI, which then processes and displays the data.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp",
						"startLine": "117",
						"endLine": "135",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"patches",
							"mPatches"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "[{\"mod\": \"test.exe\", \"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"oldbyte\": \"0x8B\", \"newbyte\": \"0x90\"}]",
					"outputDataExample": "[{\"mod\": \"test.exe\", \"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"oldbyte\": \"0x8B\", \"newbyte\": \"0x90\"}]"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f12d75be-9e3d-4205-9ea0-24222da97009",
					"diagramNodeId": "4d638c55-18c7-4008-b502-7af9c23e0e6f",
					"simStepLabel": "User Toggles a Patch",
					"simStepDescription": "The user unchecks a patch in the `PatchDialog` list. This triggers the `on_listPatches_itemChanged` slot. The function determines the new state and prepares to write the original byte back to memory to disable the patch.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp",
						"startLine": "283",
						"endLine": "318",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"on_listPatches_itemChanged",
							"item->checkState()",
							"writebyte"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"list_item_index\": 0, \"checked_state\": \"Unchecked\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"action\": \"restore_original_byte\", \"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"byte_to_write\": \"0x8B\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "a40f9118-82be-454f-ad0d-87b59878572b",
					"diagramNodeId": "0e9b11c7-de85-4006-bed5-44b08a1cf0cb",
					"simStepLabel": "GUI Requests Memory Write",
					"simStepDescription": "The event handler calls `DbgMemWrite`, sending a request to the debugger core to write the stored `oldbyte` back to the debuggee's memory at the patch address, effectively reverting the change.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/gui/Src/Gui/PatchDialog.cpp",
						"startLine": "292",
						"endLine": "292",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgMemWrite",
							"patch.patch.addr",
							"writebyte"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"data\": \"8B\", \"size\": 1}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"data\": \"8B\", \"size\": 1}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f88a7354-649b-438c-8e8a-96a1cd2938d7",
					"diagramNodeId": "1820918c-48e6-4b34-8a8f-f05bda7d0397",
					"simStepLabel": "Memory is Modified and UI is Refreshed",
					"simStepDescription": "The `DbgMemWrite` call is executed by the debugger core, modifying the target memory. The `on_listPatches_itemChanged` function then calls `GuiUpdateAllViews()` to ensure all UI components, like the Disassembly and Dump views, reflect the change.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/bridge/bridgemain.cpp",
						"startLine": "532",
						"endLine": "547",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"DbgMemWrite",
							"_dbg_memwrite"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"addr\": \"0x00401050\", \"data\": \"8B\", \"size\": 1}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"status\": \"memory_written\", \"ui_update_signaled\": true}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>Altering a program's behavior on the fly is critical for bypassing security, testing hypotheses, or fixing bugs without recompiling</li><li>- Modify program code directly in the disassembly by assembling new instructions</li><li>- Edit data in any memory region, including the stack, heap, or data sections</li><li>- Manage a list of modifications in the 'Patches' view, allowing them to be enabled, disabled, or saved to a new file</li><li>- Fill memory regions with NOP instructions to quickly disable functionality</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
				"f1e2bbd3-9c52-45af-a263-91b5e2ba4819": {
					"simStepIds": [
						"8cb6bd78-69a3-44de-890d-e07a170e6385"
					]
				},
				"5160b84c-af86-4d34-b7a8-85b6b8194c53": {
					"simStepIds": [
						"ee7c9286-ae00-4a43-8c63-0618271643da"
					]
				},
				"094d8a38-f27b-44dc-8541-09e6a9d1503a": {
					"simStepIds": [
						"4a043586-eedd-472f-b31f-6002462fd797"
					]
				},
				"4f01cd92-3313-42a1-9b82-105d775a5594": {
					"simStepIds": [
						"8d0e73e0-40e3-475d-952b-8c49dbba7c0a"
					]
				},
				"cf7957d0-3280-4735-8be7-c3a11397534b": {
					"simStepIds": [
						"98532282-a66d-4cbb-ad7d-fe8af0cfbbaa"
					]
				},
				"dfa0c3f3-92f9-4392-8dcf-a8e3017aa67a": {
					"simStepIds": [
						"b5291a29-8a69-4e54-9148-87d9fc2db162"
					]
				},
				"929af388-72f2-4739-a703-cb29da38cf95": {
